//! # GPUdb API Rust Client
//!
//! A high-performance, async Rust client for Kinetica (GPUdb) - a distributed GPU-accelerated database.
//!
//! ## Features
//!
//! - **Async/await** - Built on Tokio for non-blocking I/O
//! - **High Performance** - Achieves 600K+ records/sec with optimized bulk insert
//! - **Type Safe** - Auto-generated API from Avro schemas
//! - **Fast Avro Encoding** - Uses `serde_avro_fast` for 6-7x faster serialization
//! - **Parallel Processing** - Multi-worker architecture with rayon for encoding
//! - **Worker Distribution** - Direct routing to worker nodes for maximum throughput
//! - **Logging** - Built-in logging via the `log` crate (default level: WARN)
//!
//! ## Logging
//!
//! This library uses the [`log`](https://docs.rs/log) crate for logging. To enable logging output,
//! add a logging implementation like `env_logger` to your application:
//!
//! ```toml
//! [dependencies]
//! env_logger = "0.11"
//! ```
//!
//! Then initialize it in your main function:
//!
//! ```no_run
//! // Enable logging with default WARN level
//! env_logger::init();
//! // Or with a specific level: RUST_LOG=gpudb_api=debug cargo run
//! ```
//!
//! ### Log Levels
//!
//! Messages are logged at these levels:
//!
//! - **ERROR**: A request that could not be sent ("Giving up with an exit
//!   error after <N>ms ..."), and failures the call goes on past, such as a KiFS
//!   file that could not be transferred. Errors are also returned via
//!   `Result`.
//! - **WARN**: Failing over to another cluster, and settings that are ignored
//! - **INFO**: Failing back to the primary cluster, and KiFS files transferred
//! - **DEBUG**: Connecting, configuration details, worker setup, routing info
//! - **TRACE**: Per-batch details, HTTP request/response info (very verbose)
//!
//! The level is the application's logger's to set, for the `gpudb_api`
//! target (as with `RUST_LOG=gpudb_api=debug` above), or for all with
//! [`log::set_max_level`].
//!
//! ## Quick Start
//!
//! ```no_run
//! use gpudb_api::{
//!     Kinetica, KineticaOptions, BulkInserter, BulkInserterOptions,
//!     KineticaRecord, ShardKeyExtractor, ShardKeyValue, ShardKeyValues,
//!     avro_schema, AvroSchemaBuilder, TypePropertiesBuilder,
//! };
//! use smallvec::smallvec;
//! use std::sync::Arc;
//! use std::collections::HashMap;
//! use serde::Serialize;
//!
//! // Define your record type
//! #[derive(Serialize, Clone, Default)]
//! struct MyRecord {
//!     id: i32,
//!     name: String,
//! }
//!
//! impl ShardKeyExtractor for MyRecord {
//!     fn shard_key_values(&self) -> ShardKeyValues<'_> {
//!         smallvec![("id", ShardKeyValue::Int(self.id))]
//!     }
//! }
//!
//! impl KineticaRecord for MyRecord {
//!     fn avro_schema(&self) -> &'static str {
//!         avro_schema!(
//!             AvroSchemaBuilder::new("MyRecord")
//!                 .int_field("id")
//!                 .string_field("name")
//!         )
//!     }
//!
//!     fn type_properties() -> HashMap<String, Vec<String>> {
//!         TypePropertiesBuilder::new().build()
//!     }
//! }
//!
//! #[tokio::main]
//! async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
//!     // Create client with authentication
//!     let mut options = KineticaOptions::new();
//!     options.set_username("admin")
//!            .set_password("password")
//!            .set_use_snappy(false);
//!
//!     let kinetica = Arc::new(
//!         Kinetica::new(vec!["http://localhost:9191".to_string()], options).await?
//!     );
//!
//!     // Simple usage: Create bulk inserter with default options
//!     let inserter = BulkInserter::<MyRecord>::new(
//!         kinetica.clone(),
//!         "my_table".into(),
//!         50000,  // batch size
//!         8       // num workers
//!     ).await?;
//!
//!     // Or with options:
//!     let mut bulk_options = BulkInserterOptions::new();
//!     bulk_options.set_update_on_existing_pk(true);  // Enable upsert mode
//!
//!     let inserter_with_options = BulkInserter::<MyRecord>::with_options(
//!         kinetica,
//!         "my_table".into(),
//!         50000,
//!         8,
//!         Some(bulk_options),
//!     ).await?;
//!
//!     // Insert records...
//!
//!     Ok(())
//! }
//! ```

